# Java conventions

Mined from **20** Java microservices (the only cloned repos with `pom.xml` and
`src/main/java`) via Graphify AST + PR review mining (September 2026).
Detail: `.claude/skills/java-conventions/references/mining/pr-mining-partial-2026-09-07.md`.

The imported rules catalog (`<!-- rules-catalog:start -->` below) remains
authoritative for MUST/MUST NOT. Where this body disagrees with older
hand-written `api`/`domain`/`infra` wording, trust the repos and the catalog.

## Stack baseline

- **Java 21**, **Spring Boot** (`spring-boot-starter-parent`) — all sampled `pom.xml`
- **Group ids:** `py.com.itti`, `py.com.itti.redipro`, or `py.com.itti.ms.*`
- **Platform libs:** `py.com.itti.cc.core.spring` (`GlobalExceptionHandler`,
  `MsException`, `SpringApplicationProperties`), `py.com.itti.cc.core.common`
  (`@Track`), `itti-ms-core` utilities (e.g. `JsonUtils` — PR #4 payments-producer)
- **Common starters:** `web`, `data-jpa`, `actuator`, `test`; add `batch`,
  Kafka, WebFlux/DynamoDB per service

## Package layout — hexagonal (not `api`/`domain`/`infra`)

Root varies by bounded context — **advisory**, match the nearest sibling service:

| Pattern | Example repos |
|---|---|
| `py.com.itti.redipro.<context>` | `payments.producer`, `billing`, `acquirer.qr.confirmation` |
| `py.com.itti.redipro.ms.<context>` | `ms.qr.manager` |
| `py.com.itti.ms.<context>` | `merchant.manager`, `acquirer.ttp` |
| `py.com.ms.<context>` | `billing.data` |

| Layer | Path | Responsibility |
|---|---|---|
| Application | `application/usecase/` | Orchestration; `*UseCase` implements `domain/port/in/*InPort` |
| Application | `application/steps/` | Batch step orchestration (billing-management) |
| Application | `application/mapper/` | MapStruct / boundary mappers |
| Domain | `domain/model/`, `domain/enums/` | Entities, value objects, enums |
| Domain | `domain/port/in/`, `domain/port/out/` | Inbound/outbound ports |
| Domain | `domain/service/` | Validators, builders, domain rules |
| Domain | `domain/exceptions/` | Domain exceptions (not HTTP types) |
| Infrastructure | `infrastructure/adapter/` | Port implementations (Kafka, REST, …) |
| Infrastructure | `infrastructure/persistence/` | JPA / DynamoDB repositories |
| Infrastructure | `infrastructure/proxy/` | HTTP clients to other services |
| Infrastructure | `infrastructure/exception/` | `@RestControllerAdvice` handlers |
| Config | `config/` | Spring configuration, Kafka, etc. |

**Open question:** two repos spell the layer `infraestructure/` (billing-management,
merchant-payments); the other seven use `infrastructure/`. Match the **target
repo's existing spelling** until the owner picks one.

Controllers and REST DTOs live under `infrastructure/adapter/rest/` (or
`infrastructure/controller/`), not a top-level `api/` package.

## Naming protocol

| Kind | Pattern | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| Inbound port | `*InPort` in `domain/port/in/` | `ProcessTransactionInPort` — PR #55 qr-manager |
| Outbound port | `*Port` in `domain/port/out/` | `RetrieveCommissionPort` |
| Use case | `*UseCase` in `application/usecase/` | `ProcessTransactionUseCase` |
| Batch step | `*Step` in `application/steps/` | `UpdateBillingStep`, `SaveBillingStep` |
| Adapter | `*Adapter` | `PaymentAuditAdapter` |
| Kafka | `*KafkaConsumerAdapter`, `*KafkaProducerAdapter` | payments-producer |
| HTTP client | `*Proxy`, `*ProxyImpl` | `SellerProxy` |
| Config props | `AppProperties`, `*ConfigProperties` | God nodes: `AppProperties`, `RediproConfigProperties` |

## Policy vs advisory

Conventions mined from code start **advisory**. Promote to **policy** only when
the stack owner confirms during review. PR review threads marked **policy**
below were repeated rejections, not one-off nits.

| Convention | Status | Evidence |
|---|---|---|
| Domain/application must not import infrastructure | **Policy** | PR qr-manager, commissions; debt-recover (`@JsonProperty` on domain models) |
| Domain ports must not reference infrastructure DTOs | **Policy** | PR payment-validation (port accepting infra request type) |
| Port names identify IN vs OUT; use cases implement `*InPort` | **Policy** | PR qr-manager, payment-retry |
| Domain throws domain exceptions, not HTTP/status types | **Policy** | PR qr-manager; payment-retry, commissions |
| Logs, exceptions, and comments in **English** | **Policy** | PR payments-producer, merchant-settlement, commissions, acquirer-transactions |
| Do not swallow exceptions silently — propagate or handle explicitly | **Policy** | PR payment-validation (DynamoDB save); payment-retry (catch still returns object) |
| `@Transactional` when multiple writes must succeed or fail together | **Advisory** → likely policy | PR payment-validation (debit + payment record) |
| URLs/config via `AppProperties` / `application.yml`, not hardcoded | **Advisory** → likely policy | qr-confirmation, merchant-settlement, billing-management, debt-recover |
| Business logic in use cases/validators; queries in repositories | **Advisory** | billing-management steps |
| Kafka: do not `ack` poison messages without DLT/retry strategy | **Advisory** | PR debt-recover (`JsonProcessingException` ack) |
| DB queries must use indexes — no full table scans per transaction | **Policy** | PR acquirer-transactions |
| No hardcoded DB credentials; use env/secrets | **Policy** | PR debt-recover |
| Kafka security: consistent protocol + SASL config (not PLAINTEXT + IAM mix) | **Advisory** | PR debt-recover |
| Do not disable SSL certificate verification | **Policy** | PR billing-management |
| Seller/merchant query endpoints must scope by caller context | **Advisory** | PR merchant-manager |
| Enum names without redundant prefixes | **Advisory** | PR qr-confirmation |
| Null-check before mapper/DB handoff | **Advisory** | qr-confirmation, merchant-manager, debt-recover |
| Prefer extending existing test suites over deleting | **Advisory** | PR payment-validation |
| Avoid `public` methods added only for tests — prefer package-visible or refactor | **Advisory** | PR payment-retry |

## Configuration

- Prefer `@ConfigurationProperties` / `AppProperties` / `RediproConfigProperties`
  over scattered `@Value` — god nodes across repos
- New config keys go in `application.yml` (and profile variants), not hardcoded
  in code — PR #12 merchant-settlement
- Stage/prod URLs differ — use profile YAML, not inline `stg` strings
  (PR #4 payments-producer, PR #303 billing-management)

## Error handling

- Handlers extend `py.com.itti.cc.core.spring.exception.GlobalExceptionHandler`
  (`ControllerExceptionHandler`, `MerchantGlobalExceptionHandler`, …)
- Domain uses `domain/constants/ErrorCodes` or `domain/exceptions/*` — map to
  `MsException` in infrastructure, not `BadRequest` from domain (PR qr-manager)
- **Do not catch-and-ignore** — if infrastructure save fails, the use case must
  fail visibly (payment-validation reviews); Kafka consumers need explicit retry/DLT
  policy, not silent `ack` on parse errors (debt-recover)
- Multi-step financial writes (debit + payment record, refund + audit) → consider
  `@Transactional` on the orchestrating use case (payment-validation)
- Domain models stay free of Jackson annotations (`@JsonProperty`) — map at the
  infrastructure boundary (debt-recover, commissions)
- **Open question:** catalog cites RFC 9457 `ProblemDetail`; repos satisfy this
  via `itti-cc-core` handlers — confirm with platform team, not per-service JSON

## Domain clusters (from 20-repo sample)

High-traffic god nodes vary by bounded context — grep the target repo before
naming new types:

| Cluster | Example repos | God nodes / anchors |
|---|---|---|
| Payments / producer | payments-producer | `Transaction`, `ValidatedTransaction`, `AppProperties` |
| QR | qr-confirmation, qr-manager | `QRProviderConfirmationRequest`, `QRData` |
| Billing / settlement | billing-management, merchant-settlement, billing-data | `Billing`, `FilesMetadata` |
| Payment validation / debt | payment-validation, debt-recover, payment-retry | `PaymentTransaction`, `MerchantDebt`, `RefundTransaction` |
| Acquirer / transactions | acquirer-transactions, acquirer-data | `WebhookPayloadRequest`, `CurrencyISO4217` |
| Commissions | commissions | commission domain objects — map to request DTOs only in controller |
| Merchant | merchant-manager, merchant-payments | `MerchantVObject`, `Payment` |

## Logging

- Lombok `@Slf4j` or `@Log4j2` (both present — **open question:** pick one)
- **English** log messages and code comments in new code (PR themes above)
- No emojis in logs
- `@Track` on use cases where platform tracing applies
- No PII in logs at any level

## Kafka and async consumers

- Producer/consumer adapters in `infrastructure/adapter/message/` (payments-producer
  pattern) or dedicated listener classes (debt-recover)
- SASL/IAM via environment properties, not mixed `PLAINTEXT` + SASL blocks
  (debt-recover)
- On deserialization failure: explicit retry/DLT strategy — do not `ack` and drop
  (debt-recover)
- Include business identifiers in logs (`merchantCode`, payment id) for traceability
  (acquirer-transactions)

## Spring Boot

- Constructor injection (`@RequiredArgsConstructor`), not field `@Autowired`
- `@Transactional` on domain services / use-case layer, not controllers
- Reactive ports return `Mono`/`Flux` where the service is WebFlux-based
  (payments-producer)

## Testing

- Mirror main package under `src/test/java/`
- JUnit 5 + Mockito (`@ExtendWith(MockitoExtension.class)`)
- Colocate by layer: `application/usecase/*Test`, `domain/service/*Test`
- Object Mother / Given-When-Then per catalog `testing` rule
- Heaviest PR review focus: payment-validation, debt-recover, acquirer-transactions
  (test correctness, null handling, Mockito imports)
- Do not delete existing tests without justification (payment-validation)
- Test expectations must match production null-handling (debt-recover mapper)
- **None** — dedicated e2e module not confirmed in this sample

## Before creating anything new

1. Read `graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md` in the target repo (or run
   `graphify update . --no-cluster` locally) — place new code near **god
   nodes** (`Billing`, `Payment`, `RefundTransaction`, `PaymentTransaction`,
   `WebhookPayloadRequest`, …), don't parallel a high-traffic abstraction.
2. Grep `domain/port/out/` and `domain/port/in/` before a new integration —
   extend the existing port/adapter pair; never call `WebClient`, JPA, or
   DynamoDB from a use case without a port (PR #9 qr-manager).
3. Grep `domain/model/` and `domain/enums/` for the concept — reuse
   `EntryModeSourceEnum`, `PaymentResultEnum`, etc.; don't invent synonyms.
4. New orchestration → `application/usecase/<Verb><Noun>UseCase.java`
   implementing new `*InPort`; batch flows → `application/steps/<Name>Step.java`
   delegating to validators/use cases (billing-management pattern).
5. New external system → `*Port` + `infrastructure/adapter/` or
   `infrastructure/proxy/`; DTOs stay in infrastructure, not `domain/model/`.
6. New config → `application.yml` + properties class; path constants in
   `ApiConstants` or `AppProperties`, not string literals in business code.
7. Before adding a file, find the nearest analogous class in the **same layer**
   and match its package spelling (`infrastructure` vs `infraestructure`).
8. If Graphify shows an existing builder/validator on the path (e.g.
   `ValidatedTransactionBuilder` → `ValidatedTransactionMapper`), extend it —
   ask rather than fork.

